{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1207, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an array nums of length n. You are also given an integer k.\nYou perform the following operation on nums once:\n\nSelect a subarray nums[i..j] where 0 <= i <= j <= n - 1.\nSelect an integer x and add x to all the elements in nums[i..j].\n\nFind the maximum frequency of the value k after the operation.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4,5,6], k = 1\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\nAfter adding -5 to nums[2..5], 1 has a frequency of 2 in [1, 2, -2, -1, 0, 1].\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [10,2,3,4,5,5,4,3,2,2], k = 10\nOutput: 4\nExplanation:\nAfter adding 8 to nums[1..9], 10 has a frequency of 4 in [10, 10, 11, 12, 13, 13, 12, 11, 10, 10].\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= n == nums.length <= 10^5\n1 <= nums[i] <= 50\n1 <= k <= 50\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def maxFrequency(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1256, "char_start": 1219, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\n1\nOutput:\n2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1319, "char_start": 1268, "quote": "Input:\n[10, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5, 4, 3, 2, 2]\n10\nOutput:\n4", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "d302950e07d212579fe2ade986da94ecd4892bdf48ebac7cd2af7426628842df", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "18a30c9227ecb6717916b16d35c4b2b9f84cc1f88262bd2c7d999f71d5f3b6f8", "seq": 2}
